[BEGIN]
  ObjTp=Hd
  Cmn1=INPUTS\\Clear_Output_On_Filter_Matched: this will set Value_Filtered||1
  Cmn2=to zero, if this signal is HIGH & Value_To_Filter's current state||1
  Cmn3=is within the FilterList.\\		NOTE: THIS TAKES PRECEDENCE OVER NewValueFor[n].
  Cmn4=||1if this signal is HIGH, then the number change wont happen.\\\\
  Cmn5=Filter_Number: analog value determining the rooms "mode" and which||1
  Cmn6=Items should be visible in that mode, based on the paramter list||1
  Cmn7=associated with that output\\Value_To_Filter: a number we wish to||1
  Cmn8=check for values that could cause trouble if passed. think VTC getting||1
  Cmn9=sent as a program audio source\\\\OUTPUTS\\Value_Filtered: the filtered||1
  Cmn10=value, which will either change, if using the \\\\PARAMETERS\\\\
  Cmn11=Filter_List: a list of values you dont want to get passed to the||1
  Cmn12=output(you dont need a delimiter but for readability use commas,||1
  Cmn13=i.e 1,2,3,5)\\             NOTE: dont put any values you want to||1
  Cmn14=change here. \\\\NewValueFor[n]: a new value you want to change||1
  Cmn15=[n] to.\\	i.e = on a DMPS to select the AirMedia as a video source,||1
  Cmn16=you must select 9, however if you want it as an audio source, you||1
  Cmn17=must select 14. (stupid i know.)\\		  you would increment the parameter||1
  Cmn18=list, until you reach 9, and then enter the value 14 in its field.
  Cmn19=||1anytime 9 comes in to this module (provided it is not in the filter||1
  Cmn20=list)\\          it will be changed to 14\\	NOTE = use this "" for||1
  Cmn21=unused parameters. if you want only certain values to be set to||1
  Cmn22=zero use 0d
[END]
